---
/**
 * The first of Rahul's two output panels — sheet 2's own title, and the reason
 * the sheet exists: *Income Computation*, separate from the tax working, so the
 * reader follows gross income through to taxable income before a rate touches
 * anything.
 *
 * Design settled before the component in `TaxIncomeComputation.checks.md`.
 *
 * Its shape is the FORM'S shape, deliberately. The slab pot first — what clubs
 * — then the gains taxed on their own terms, because a reader who has just
 * filled in three blocks should recognise the arithmetic as those three blocks
 * read back to them rather than as a second taxonomy they have to learn.
 *
 * Every row here is written by the page's one script from one engine result.
 * The rows that carry no figure are removed rather than shown at nil, so the
 * panel is as long as the reader's own year and no longer.
 */
---

<section
  id="taxIncomeComputation"
  class="rounded-2xl border border-navy-200 dark:border-white/10 bg-white dark:bg-navy-900/40 p-5 sm:p-6 space-y-4"
  aria-label="How your income becomes taxable income"
>
  <div class="space-y-1">
    <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100">Income computation</h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400 leading-relaxed">
      What you earned, what the law lets you take off it, and what is left to be taxed.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="overflow-x-auto">
    <table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
      <thead>
        <tr class="border-b border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-800 text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">
          <th class="py-2 font-semibold">Item</th>
          <th id="incColNew" class="py-2 text-right font-semibold w-28">New regime</th>
          <th id="incColOld" class="py-2 text-right font-semibold w-28">Old regime</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <!--
        One tbody, filled row by row from the engine result. It is built rather
        than pre-written because a row exists only when it carries a figure, and
        because the Chapter VI-A lines are one per section the reader actually
        claimed — there is no fixed set of them to lay out in advance.
      -->
      <tbody
        id="incRows"
        class="divide-y divide-navy-200 dark:divide-navy-800 text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100"
      ></tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <!--
    The one thing this panel says in words rather than in figures: where a claim
    was cut, and by what. sol-056 returns a line per section carrying claimed,
    allowed, the ceiling that applied and the reason, which is what these notes
    are made of. A reader whose four lakh of 80C became one and a half is told
    so where it happened (dd-009/dont-1).
  -->
  <div id="incNotes" class="space-y-2 empty:hidden"></div>
</section>
